/-! ## Layer 11: automorphisms -/

/-- **Finiteness of the automorphism group when the geometric genus is positive** (Layer 11,
the headline finiteness theorem; Rosenlicht, Trans. Amer. Math. Soc. 79 (1955), §3, p. 5, with
§2, Theorem, p. 4). Let `F / k` be a function field with exact constants and genus `g ≥ 2` over an
arbitrary field `k`, let `K` be an algebraic closure of `k` and let `F'` be generated by `F` and
`K`. If `F' / K` has positive genus, then `F` has finitely many `k`-automorphisms.

Exactness makes the nilradical of `F ⊗[k] K` its only prime ideal and `F'` its residue field, so
every automorphism of `F` extends to `F'`. If `g(F' / K) ≥ 2` this is Rosenlicht's theorem over
the algebraically closed `K`. If `g(F' / K) = 1`, infinitely many automorphisms would make `F / k`
separably generated, so a subgroup of finite index would fix a place of `F'` over one of the
finitely many places of `F` at which the regular model is not smooth, and the automorphisms of a
genus-one field fixing a place are finitely many.

Both genus hypotheses are load-bearing. Over a separably closed imperfect field of
characteristic `p ≥ 5`, `k(x, y)` with `y ^ p - y = a x ^ p` and `a ∉ k ^ p` has exact constants,
genus `(p - 1)(p - 2) / 2 ≥ 6` and infinitely many automorphisms `x ↦ x + β`, `y ↦ y + α` with
`α ^ p - α = a β ^ p` (Rosenlicht, §3); over `K` it becomes `K(y - a ^ (1 / p) x)`, of genus `0`.
An elliptic function field over `ℚ` with a point of infinite order has infinitely many
translations, and genus `1` both over `ℚ` and over `ℚ̄`. -/
theorem finite_algEquiv_of_two_le_genus_of_genus_constantCompositum_pos {k : Type u}
    {K : Type u'} {F : Type v} {F' : Type v'} [Field k] [Field K] [Field F] [Field F']
    [Algebra k K] [Algebra k F] [Algebra k F'] [Algebra K F'] [Algebra F F']
    [IsScalarTower k K F'] [IsScalarTower k F F'] [IsAlgClosure k K]
    (hF : TauCeti.IsFunctionField k F) (hex : IsIntegrallyClosedIn k F)
    (hc : TauCeti.constantCompositum F K F' = ⊤) (hg : 2 ≤ TauCeti.genus k F)
    (hK : 0 < TauCeti.genus K F') :
    Finite (F ≃ₐ[k] F) :=
  sorry

/-- **Finiteness of the automorphism group in genus at least two over a perfect field** (Layer 11,
the perfect-field case of
`finite_algEquiv_of_two_le_genus_of_genus_constantCompositum_pos`): over a perfect field `k`, a
function field `F / k` with exact constants and genus `g ≥ 2` has finitely many
`k`-automorphisms, in every characteristic. Over perfect `k` with exact constants, `F / k` is
separably generated, so `F ⊗[k] k̄` is a domain, algebraic over `F` and hence a field `F'`; since
`k̄ / k` is separable, `F' / k̄` keeps the genus `g` (the pinned
`TauCeti.genus_eq_genus_of_constantCompositum_eq_top`), which is positive.

The genus hypothesis is load-bearing: `Aut(k(x) / k) ≅ PGL₂(k)` is infinite for infinite `k`, and
translations make the automorphism group infinite in genus `1` over an algebraically closed field.
Perfectness cannot be dropped without a replacement: Rosenlicht's exceptional fields over
separably closed imperfect fields, recalled at the general theorem, have infinitely many
automorphisms. -/
theorem finite_algEquiv_of_two_le_genus {k : Type u} {F : Type v} [Field k] [Field F]
    [Algebra k F] [PerfectField k] (hF : TauCeti.IsFunctionField k F)
    (hex : IsIntegrallyClosedIn k F) (hg : 2 ≤ TauCeti.genus k F) :
    Finite (F ≃ₐ[k] F) :=
  sorry

end TauCetiRoadmap.AlgebraicCurves

